  "apps": [
    {
      "name": "pixel-press",
      "description": "Open-source, local-first desktop video compressor. Uses on-device LLM inference (llama.cpp + SmolLM2-360M GGUF) to translate plain-language intent into FFmpeg encode plans. Built with Tauri (Rust + React), shipping via GitHub Releases for macOS and Linux.",
      "image": "pixel-press-logo.png",
      "technologies": [
        {
          "name": "Rust",
          "description": "Native backend and Tauri integration.",
          "level": "9/10"
        },
        {
          "name": "React/TypeScript",
          "description": "Desktop UI with Tailwind and shadcn/ui.",
          "level": "9/10"
        },
        {
          "name": "llama.cpp",
          "description": "On-device GGUF inference for intent parsing.",
          "level": "8/10"
        }
      ],
      "platforms": [
        {
          "name": "macOS",
          "type": "desktop",
          "url": "https://github.com/GAM3RG33K/pixel-press/releases"
        },
        {
          "name": "Linux",
          "type": "desktop",
          "url": "https://github.com/GAM3RG33K/pixel-press/releases"
        }
      ],
      "downloads": "",
      "link": "https://github.com/GAM3RG33K/pixel-press",
      "slug": "pixel-press",
      "tagline": "Local-first, offline video compressor with on-device LLM inference",
      "status": "In active development",
      "journey": [
        "Built because no existing compressor respects your files \u2014 pixel-press runs 100% on-device: FFmpeg runs as a native subprocess, and a tiny local LLM (SmolLM2-360M, GGUF via llama.cpp) turns plain-language intent like \u201csmallest file\u201d or \u201ckeep the subs, strip audio\u201d into real FFmpeg plans.",
        "Technical bet: inference runs fully local (no browser WASM, no in-browser LLM) \u2014 a Tauri v2 shell bridges a Rust backend to a React + Tailwind UI. An optional rule engine is the default path, so the app works with zero AI downloaded.",
        "CI release pipeline ships DMG and AppImage/.deb for macOS and Linux on tag push. In active development \u2014 not yet presented as a shipped product with users."
      ],
      "highlights": [
        "On-device LLM intent parsing with schema-constrained output + rule-engine fallback",
        "Zero-copy output handling \u2014 encoded files never enter the webview",
        "Huge-file smart probe: native path-based encode for multi-GB sources",
        "GitHub Actions release pipeline: 4 shipping targets, tag-push triggered"
      ]
    },
